§ `Legal Identity of Defendants (Organisational Child Abuse) Act 2018 -- questions for the survivor`

§§ `Does the Act help me? (ss 3-6)`
-- Situation: you were abused as a child, and the organisation responsible is not incorporated.

@export Is what happened to me "child abuse" under the Legal Identity of Defendants (Organisational Child Abuse) Act 2018 (Vic) (s 3)? Physical or sexual abuse while you were a minor, with any psychological abuse arising from it; what you allege counts.
GIVEN `my age at the time` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age, in years, when the abuse happened (or began)
      `what was done to me` IS A `Kind of conduct` @desc Was it sexual assault or other sexual misconduct; physical abuse; force with a lawful justification or excuse (or another lawful use of force); psychological abuse alone, not arising from physical or sexual abuse; or other harm, such as neglect?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is what happened to me child abuse under the Act` `my age at the time` `what was done to me` MEANS
    `s 3 -- it is child abuse` `my age at the time` `what was done to me`

@export Is the organisation an "NGO" under the Act: a non-government organisation that is an unincorporated association or body (s 5)? It need not have a written constitution or fixed membership.
GIVEN `it is a non-government organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the organisation a non-government organisation (not a government department, agency or public body)?
      `it is unincorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an unincorporated association or body (not a company, incorporated association or other body with its own legal identity)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the organisation an NGO under the Act` `it is a non-government organisation` `it is unincorporated` MEANS
    `s 5 -- it is an NGO` `it is a non-government organisation` `it is unincorporated`

@export Is this trust an "associated trust" of the organisation, one it uses to conduct its activities and controls (ss 3, 6)?
GIVEN `it uses the trust to conduct its activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the organisation use the trust to conduct its activities?
      `it controls the trust's income or property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the organisation, directly or indirectly, the power to control how the trust's income is applied or its property distributed?
      `it can take the benefit of the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the organisation the power to obtain the beneficial enjoyment of the trust's property or income, with or without anyone else's consent?
      `it can appoint or remove the trustees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the organisation, directly or indirectly, the power to appoint or remove the trustee or trustees?
      `it can appoint or remove beneficiaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the organisation, directly or indirectly, the power to appoint or remove beneficiaries of the trust?
      `the trustee follows its wishes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trustee accustomed, or under a formal or informal obligation, to act on the organisation's directions, instructions or wishes?
      `it decides other matters about the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the organisation, directly or indirectly, the power to determine the outcome of any other decisions about the trust's operations?
      `a member holds such a power under the deed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a member, or a management committee member, of the organisation have any of those powers under the trust deed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is this trust an associated trust of the organisation` `it uses the trust to conduct its activities` `it controls the trust's income or property` `it can take the benefit of the trust` `it can appoint or remove the trustees` `it can appoint or remove beneficiaries` `the trustee follows its wishes` `it decides other matters about the trust` `a member holds such a power under the deed` MEANS
    `s 3 -- it is an associated trust` `it uses the trust to conduct its activities` (`s 6 -- the NGO controls the trust` `it controls the trust's income or property` `it can take the benefit of the trust` `it can appoint or remove the trustees` `it can appoint or remove beneficiaries` `the trustee follows its wishes` `it decides other matters about the trust` `a member holds such a power under the deed`)

@export Does the Act apply to the organisation I want to sue (s 4(2))? It does if it is an NGO, my claim is founded on child abuse, it could be sued and found liable but for being unincorporated, and it controls at least one associated trust. The abuse may have happened at any time (s 4(3)).
GIVEN `my age at the time` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age, in years, when the abuse happened (or began)
      `what was done to me` IS A `Kind of conduct` @desc Was it sexual assault or other sexual misconduct; physical abuse; force with a lawful justification or excuse; psychological abuse alone; or other harm, such as neglect?
      `it is a non-government organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the organisation a non-government organisation?
      `it is unincorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an unincorporated association or body?
      `a court would find it liable if it were incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Leaving aside that it is unincorporated, would the organisation be capable of being sued and found liable for your claim?
      `it uses and controls at least one trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the organisation use at least one trust to conduct its activities, and control it (see the associated-trust question)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does the Act apply to the organisation I want to sue` `my age at the time` `what was done to me` `it is a non-government organisation` `it is unincorporated` `a court would find it liable if it were incorporated` `it uses and controls at least one trust` MEANS
    `s 4(2) -- the Act applies to the NGO` (`s 3 -- it is child abuse` `my age at the time` `what was done to me`) (`s 5 -- it is an NGO` `it is a non-government organisation` `it is unincorporated`) `a court would find it liable if it were incorporated` `it uses and controls at least one trust`

§§ `Whom do I sue? (ss 7, 8, 13)`
-- Situation: the Act applies to the organisation, and you have started, or want to start, a proceeding.

@export Whom do I sue: the organisation in its own name, the entity it nominated, or the trustees of its associated trust (ss 7(2), 8(5), 13)? Answers nothing if the Act does not apply to the organisation.
GIVEN `the Act applies to the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act apply to the organisation (the s 4(2) question)?
      `it has nominated a proper defendant who consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the organisation nominated an entity to be the proper defendant, with that entity's consent?
      `the nominee can be sued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the nominated entity capable of being sued (for example a company or incorporated body)? Any answer if there is no nomination.
      `the court has ordered my claim to proceed against the trustees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court ordered under s 8(4) that your claim proceed against the trustees of an associated trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Defendant`
`Whom do I sue` `the Act applies to the organisation` `it has nominated a proper defendant who consented` `the nominee can be sued` `the court has ordered my claim to proceed against the trustees` MEANS
    `ss 7, 8, 13 -- the defendant to sue` `the Act applies to the organisation` `it has nominated a proper defendant who consented` `the nominee can be sued` `the court has ordered my claim to proceed against the trustees`

@export Can I start, or carry on, my proceeding against the organisation in its own name, though it is unincorporated (s 13)? Yes until a proper defendant is nominated or appointed; no after that.
GIVEN `the Act applies to the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act apply to the organisation (the s 4(2) question)?
      `a proper defendant is in place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a proper defendant been nominated (with consent) or appointed by the court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I sue the organisation in its own name` `the Act applies to the organisation` `a proper defendant is in place` MEANS
    `s 13 -- the proceeding may be commenced or continue against the NGO in its own name` `the Act applies to the organisation` `a proper defendant is in place`

@export By when can the organisation nominate a proper defendant to my claim (s 7(3))? 120 days after the proceeding commenced, unless the court orders otherwise.
GIVEN `the day my proceeding commenced` IS A DATE @desc The day you commenced the proceeding (ISO date, e.g. 2026-03-02)
      `the court has ordered a different time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court ordered a different time for the nomination?
      `the last day the court allowed` IS A DATE @desc If so, the last day the court allowed (any date otherwise)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when can the organisation nominate a proper defendant` `the day my proceeding commenced` `the court has ordered a different time` `the last day the court allowed` MEANS
    `s 7(3) -- the last day for the NGO to nominate a proper defendant` `the day my proceeding commenced` `the court has ordered a different time` `the last day the court allowed`

@export Can I apply to the court for my claim to proceed against the trustees of the organisation's associated trust (s 8(1), (2))? Yes if no proper defendant was nominated within 120 days of commencement, or the nominee cannot be sued or lacks the assets to meet a judgment. The application is by summons (Supreme Court Rules r 85.04).
GIVEN `the Act applies to the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act apply to the organisation (the s 4(2) question)?
      `the day my proceeding commenced` IS A DATE @desc The day you commenced the proceeding (ISO date)
      `the day I would apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you would apply to the court (ISO date)
      `it has nominated a proper defendant who consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the organisation nominated a proper defendant, with that entity's consent?
      `the day of the nomination` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it nominated (any date otherwise)
      `the nominee can be sued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the nominated entity capable of being sued? Any answer if there is no nomination.
      `a court would find the nominee lacks the assets to meet a judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the court find that the nominee does not have sufficient assets or property to meet any judgment or order in your proceeding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I apply for my claim to proceed against the trustees of an associated trust` `the Act applies to the organisation` `the day my proceeding commenced` `the day I would apply` `it has nominated a proper defendant who consented` `the day of the nomination` `the nominee can be sued` `a court would find the nominee lacks the assets to meet a judgment` MEANS
    `s 8(1) -- section 8 applies to the claim` `the Act applies to the organisation` `the day my proceeding commenced` `the day I would apply` `it has nominated a proper defendant who consented` `the day of the nomination` `the nominee can be sued` `a court would find the nominee lacks the assets to meet a judgment`

@export On my application under s 8, must the organisation identify its associated trusts (s 8(3))? Answers nothing if s 8 does not apply to my claim.
GIVEN `I can apply under section 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does s 8 apply to your claim (the previous question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the organisation identify its associated trusts` `I can apply under section 8` MEANS
    `s 8(3) -- the NGO bears the onus of identifying its associated trusts` `I can apply under section 8`

@export Once a proper defendant is in place, must the organisation itself still meet its obligations in running the proceeding, such as interlocutory steps (ss 7(5), 8(9))? Answers nothing while the organisation is itself the defendant.
GIVEN `a proper defendant is in place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a proper defendant been nominated (with consent) or appointed by the court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the organisation still meet its obligations in the proceeding` `a proper defendant is in place` MEANS
    `ss 7(5), 8(9) -- the NGO keeps its obligations in the conduct of the proceeding` `a proper defendant is in place`

§§ `The steps after a nomination (Supreme Court Rules Order 85)`
-- Situation: your proceeding is in the Supreme Court and the organisation has nominated a proper defendant.

@export By when must the organisation serve its nomination of a proper defendant on me (Supreme Court Rules r 85.02(2))? 7 days after it is filed, leaving out 24 December to 9 January, moved to a weekday if it falls on a weekend (public holidays are not counted).
GIVEN `the day the nomination was filed` IS A DATE @desc The day the nomination (Form 85A) was filed with the Prothonotary (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the organisation serve its nomination on me` `the day the nomination was filed` MEANS
    `r 85.02(2) -- the last day for the NGO to serve its nomination` `the day the nomination was filed`

@export By when must I file an amended originating process and statement of claim naming the proper defendant (Supreme Court Rules r 85.03)? 28 days after the nomination is served on you, leaving out 24 December to 9 January; service after 4 pm or on a weekend counts from the next weekday; a last day on a weekend moves to the Monday (public holidays are not counted).
GIVEN `the day the nomination was served on me` IS A DATE @desc The day the nomination was served on you (ISO date)
      `it was served after 4 pm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it served after 4.00 pm?
      `the court has directed a different time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court directed a different time?
      `the last day the court directed` IS A DATE @desc If so, the last day the court directed (any date otherwise)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I file my amended originating process and statement of claim` `the day the nomination was served on me` `it was served after 4 pm` `the court has directed a different time` `the last day the court directed` MEANS
    `r 85.03 -- the last day for the plaintiff to file the amended originating process and statement of claim` `the day the nomination was served on me` `it was served after 4 pm` `the court has directed a different time` `the last day the court directed`

§§ `Getting paid (ss 9-12)`
-- Situation: there is a proper defendant, and you have (or expect) a judgment.

@export What is the most I can recover from the trustees of one associated trust (s 9(2))? Their liability, costs included, is limited to the value of the trust property.
GIVEN `my judgment and costs` IS A NUMBER @desc The judgment (or the amount you expect) with costs, in dollars
      `the value of the trust property` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of the associated trust's property, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can recover from the trustees of one associated trust` `my judgment and costs` `the value of the trust property` MEANS
    `s 9(2) -- the most recoverable from the trustees of one associated trust` `my judgment and costs` `the value of the trust property`

@export May the trustees of the associated trust pay my judgment out of the trust property, whatever the trust deed or any other law says, without being in breach of trust (ss 9(1), 11)? Answers nothing unless the trustees are a proper defendant and the liability arose in your claim.
GIVEN `the trustees are a proper defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the trustees of the associated trust a proper defendant to your claim (nominated under s 7 or appointed under s 8)?
      `the liability arose in my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability one incurred in your claim because they are the proper defendant (including an unpaid judgment debt)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May the trustees pay my judgment from the trust property` `the trustees are a proper defendant` `the liability arose in my claim` MEANS
    `ss 9(1), 11 -- the trustees may pay the liability from trust property whatever the trust deed says` `the trustees are a proper defendant` `the liability arose in my claim`

@export Can the proper defendant rely on a defence or immunity against my claim (s 10)? Yes, any the organisation would have had as a defendant had it been incorporated; answers nothing for any other.
GIVEN `a proper defendant is in place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a proper defendant (nominated under s 7 or appointed under s 8)?
      `the organisation would have had the defence if incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the defence or immunity have been available to the organisation as a defendant had it been incorporated?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the proper defendant rely on the defence` `a proper defendant is in place` `the organisation would have had the defence if incorporated` MEANS
    `s 10 -- the proper defendant may rely on the defence` `a proper defendant is in place` `the organisation would have had the defence if incorporated`

@export Does the organisation's insurance against child abuse damages cover the proper defendant too (s 12)? The organisation keeps its own cover.
GIVEN `the organisation is insured for such damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the organisation a right to be indemnified under an insurance policy for damages awarded in a child abuse claim?
      `a proper defendant is in place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a proper defendant (nominated under s 7 or appointed under s 8)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the organisation's insurance cover the proper defendant` `the organisation is insured for such damages` `a proper defendant is in place` MEANS
    `s 12 -- the NGO's insurance extends to the proper defendant` `the organisation is insured for such damages` `a proper defendant is in place`

§§ `Read with other Victorian law`
-- Situation: you are working out the duty you rely on and the time you have.

@export Does the organisation owe me the Wrongs Act 1958 Part XIII duty, as a "relevant organisation" under s 88(ba) (an NGO capable of being sued under this Act)? Answers nothing for abuse before 1 July 2017 (s 93); no means s 88(ba) does not make it one.
GIVEN `the day of the abuse` IS A DATE @desc The day the abuse happened (or began) (ISO date)
      `it is organised for some end, purpose or work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the organisation organised for some end, purpose or work (a church, club, school, charity and the like)?
      `it has care, supervision or authority over children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it exercise care, supervision or authority over children, as part of its main activities or otherwise?
      `the Act applies to the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does this Act apply to the organisation (the s 4(2) question)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the organisation a relevant organisation under the Wrongs Act` `the day of the abuse` `it is organised for some end, purpose or work` `it has care, supervision or authority over children` `the Act applies to the organisation` MEANS
    `Wrongs Act s 88(ba), s 93 -- the NGO is a relevant organisation` `the day of the abuse` `it is organised for some end, purpose or work` `it has care, supervision or authority over children` `the Act applies to the organisation`

@export Can I bring my action at any time, with no limitation period (Limitation of Actions Act 1958 ss 27O, 27P)? Yes for personal injury from physical or sexual abuse as a minor; no for a dependants' death claim under Wrongs Act Part III (3 years from discoverability, s 27Q); nothing outside Division 5.
GIVEN `my action is for death or personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action for personal injury (or a death) resulting from the abuse?
      `my age at the time` IS A NUMBER @desc The injured person's age, in years, when the abuse happened (or began)
      `what was done` IS A `Kind of conduct` @desc Was it sexual assault or other sexual misconduct; physical abuse; lawful force; psychological abuse alone; or other harm, such as neglect?
      `it is a dependants' claim for a death under Wrongs Act Part III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action a claim by dependants for a death, under Part III of the Wrongs Act 1958?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I bring my action at any time` `my action is for death or personal injury` `my age at the time` `what was done` `it is a dependants' claim for a death under Wrongs Act Part III` MEANS
    `Limitation Act ss 27O, 27P -- the action may be brought at any time` `my action is for death or personal injury` `my age at the time` `what was done` `it is a dependants' claim for a death under Wrongs Act Part III`
